.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH auth 1  "auth " 
.SH NAME
auth \- Manage credentials for IronForge hosts
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBauth\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage credentials for IronForge hosts
.PP
Tokens are personal access tokens created in the web UI (Settings → Tokens). `auth login` reads one from a no\-echo prompt on a terminal, or from stdin with `\-\-with\-token`/a pipe. `token_store = "keyring"` in the config keeps the token out of the config file. `auth git\-credential` implements the git credential helper protocol so `git clone`/`push` reuse the same token.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
auth\-login(1)
Log in with a personal access token (validates it against /users/me)
.TP
auth\-status(1)
List configured hosts, token prefixes and usable scopes
.TP
auth\-logout(1)
Remove local credentials (the token stays valid server\-side)
.TP
auth\-token(1)
Print the token of the resolved host (for scripts)
.TP
auth\-git\-credential(1)
git credential helper: answer `get` for configured hosts only (protocol and host must both match). Configure it for your host only: git config \-\-global credential.https://HOST.helper "!ifg auth git\-credential"
.TP
auth\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
